Notebook[{
Cell["WolframExample: Rust libraries from the Wolfram Language", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"9eb3e47c-79ef-471a-b09f-2ce9c861bb61"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook exercises the WolframExample paclet, whose functions are \
implemented in Rust (see WolframExample/Libs). Evaluate it top to bottom.

If the setup section reports a missing paclet, build the library first:
    cd WolframExample && cargo wl build\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"65a3c856-262f-4ff5-a0cd-1851244bc5ed"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c658dd3e-3443-47d8-ab86-b1a73fe73b53"],

Cell["\<\
Both paclets \[AHat]\.80\.94 the hand-written WolframExample and the \
generated WolframExampleLib \[AHat]\.80\.94 sit in this notebook's parent \
directory, so one PacletDirectoryLoad registers both.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cd7bd11d-f740-4173-b9c7-fdfac168b895"],

Cell["PacletDirectoryLoad[ParentDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]]]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"e00743e2-e8ca-479a-9b9b-0c865dea1944"],

Cell["PacletObject[\"WolframExample\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"83c541ad-8d48-46f9-8369-f1d6772456c9"],

Cell["\<\
The library paclet holds nothing but the compiled dylibs and a generated \
Functions.wl loader:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c7713752-0d54-4110-9fbe-e252864b19c2"],

Cell["PacletObject[\"WolframExampleLib\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"e92fc36e-2583-401a-8565-4130fa77c701"],

Cell["Needs[\"WolframExample`\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"6e0df02e-68d9-40f8-8d9d-0dfd41d16449"],

Cell["Everything the package exports:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"598eb5ae-f7e0-41e9-82c8-16f91bc6ceeb"],

Cell["?WolframExample`*", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a8f686a7-bbf9-4554-86f0-84f8f20345d1"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Math", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"4b0b9489-1a9f-4006-a1cd-528fb9115429"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Scalars and arrays", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"da69b643-7f24-4385-9223-b3e993a1d7cf"],

Cell["\<\
A plain Rust function over two f64s. Arguments and result cross as raw \
MArgument scalars \[AHat]\.80\.94 no serialization at all.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d1ac772e-04d7-4d08-bdd5-b7e998d2f25d"],

Cell["ExampleAdd[2, 3]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"dc64a151-7b9d-4801-8fef-a62dadb2010b"],

Cell["\<\
NumericArrays are read zero-copy: Rust sees the kernel's own memory, no copy \
and no conversion. Lists are packed into a Real64 NumericArray by the wrapper \
first.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"341ba47d-7330-4a73-92c7-9050f37592e8"],

Cell["ExampleDot[{1, 2, 3}, {4, 5, 6}]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"db70e140-246a-4f96-bbc9-5d0ebb4bcd19"],

Cell["\<\
ExampleDot[
    NumericArray[Range[1., 100000.], \"Real64\"],
    NumericArray[Range[100000., 1., -1.], \"Real64\"]
]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"17ab50f2-fbb2-4c89-a1ef-0efc8a6109e4"],

Cell["Same call, timed against the kernel's own Dot:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2c85c472-a4b1-4130-8b34-34ae9a12e84e"],

Cell["\<\
With[{a = Range[1., 100000.], b = Range[100000., 1., -1.]},
    {
        \"Rust\" -> First @ RepeatedTiming @ ExampleDot[a, b],
        \"Kernel\" -> First @ RepeatedTiming @ Dot[a, b]
    }
]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"05dd3cf9-8f94-437e-82b8-30510bee806c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Structs and enums", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"1ad5ef06-43d2-44cb-8d3b-2d6f783ce014"],

Cell["\<\
Structured arguments cross as WXF. A Rust struct is an Association keyed by \
its field names; the wrapper here presents Wolfram-style capitalized keys.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3fad4f87-187a-451b-8a3d-17dd3ff64532"],

Cell["ExampleSymmetricPoint[<|\"X\" -> 10, \"Y\" -> 20|>]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"7eccd878-c758-48c0-bad5-4f92decafaac"],

Cell["\<\
ExampleArea goes through a Rust enum \[AHat]\.80\.94 one function, one match, \
two shapes:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c171f60e-c745-4cbc-95d0-032031c7cc54"],

Cell["ExampleArea[<|\"Radius\" -> 1|>]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"239ac424-e26b-46a3-ad11-9334fc18deb8"],

Cell["ExampleArea[<|\"Width\" -> 10, \"Height\" -> 20|>]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"d8551021-8cb3-4610-bbde-d87d1459dd00"],

Cell["Table[ExampleArea[<|\"Radius\" -> r|>], {r, 1, 5}]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"fd2e32b7-b479-42af-b9bc-adfcf2e8ca0c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Errors", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"a5fb330f-88ce-4b39-a00e-8dcd055e5189"],

Cell["\<\
A Rust Result<f64, String> comes back as {\"Ok\", value} or {\"Err\", \
message}; the wrapper turns the error branch into a Failure.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8876d517-7ef3-467b-8496-7aa4beea182d"],

Cell["ExampleSafeDivide[10, 4]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"e1783f07-03e2-4c5b-911d-a5087a348403"],

Cell["ExampleSafeDivide[1, 0]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"52d273a2-03eb-41d9-9900-f7d6d12d03ad"],

Cell["So the usual Failure handling applies:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3e0f3bde-ae87-451f-8638-74e8b76e8296"],

Cell["\<\
FailureQ /@ {ExampleSafeDivide[1, 2], ExampleSafeDivide[1, 0]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"7b3f25bf-0e22-4e0e-8ced-559ae0c07931"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["DuckDB", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e6ad34ff-9c67-47dd-bed5-58e23deaa3d4"],

Cell["\<\
An entire embedded SQL engine, statically linked into the library \[AHat]\.80\
\.94 nothing to install. Query results come back as Arrow and are decoded \
into a Tabular.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7cc6ef60-d3e9-4661-9c16-70c056e8fc37"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Scoped connections", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"924fc287-7f17-4c99-bb6c-06a2cab48fbf"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute opens a connection, applies the function to it, and closes it \
again \[AHat]\.80\.94 even if the body fails.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"572cd726-9f68-43d9-9ecb-23e06416f8b2"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb://\", DuckDBQuery[#, \"SELECT 42 AS answer\"] &]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"3fab2036-9ddd-4f0f-a844-2a22afd432b4"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb://\", DuckDBQuery[#,
    \"SELECT n::INTEGER AS id,
            (n * 1.5)::DOUBLE AS score,
            'item_' || n AS label,
            n % 2 = 0 AS is_even
     FROM generate_series(1, 5) t(n)\"] &]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"fb821890-1591-49a3-81e4-4a5fd525f7a4"],

Cell["\<\
The result is an ordinary Tabular, so the usual operations work:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"803cd196-ca5a-4610-bfa2-02b826af1229"],

Cell["\<\
tab = DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb://\", DuckDBQuery[#,
    \"SELECT n FROM generate_series(1, 100) t(n)\"] &];
{Length[tab], Total[tab[[All, \"n\"]]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c02d3061-120b-44c9-a4c9-fa842361386d"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Parameters", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"7dc83a69-6a7a-46b8-8d0a-fd18c3de0bba"],

Cell["\<\
Values are bound to the ? placeholders in order, so nothing is interpolated \
into the SQL string.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d699c564-cd1b-4f8b-8aa1-b8ab49a92278"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb://\", DuckDBQuery[#,
    \"SELECT n FROM generate_series(1, 5) t(n) WHERE n > ?\", {2}] &]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"976a242b-fa5d-40db-ad0d-32087037dffe"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb://\", DuckDBQuery[#,
    \"SELECT ?::INTEGER + ?::INTEGER AS total\", {20, 22}] &]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"36401362-27a0-40f5-9d34-6649686bdfe1"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Explicit connections", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"fe9e798c-1203-4d8b-9c22-7f9ae5ddcfc3"],

Cell["\<\
For several statements against the same database, hold the handle yourself. \
Here an on-disk file, which persists after disconnecting.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bd449376-e5d4-44a9-a6c0-6bbcee224062"],

Cell["\<\
file = FileNameJoin[{$TemporaryDirectory, \"wolfram-example.duckdb\"}];
Quiet[DeleteFile[file]];
conn = DuckDBConnect[\"duckdb:///\" <> file]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"6dc5bc6f-fcfd-4e73-86f4-0e221325be34"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBQuery[conn,
    \"CREATE TABLE fruit AS SELECT * FROM (VALUES (1, 'apple'), (2, 'pear')) \
v(id, name)\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"3ac87f53-7ecf-4411-aac7-e23e2e92f4b7"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBQuery[conn, \"INSERT INTO fruit VALUES (?, ?)\", {3, \"plum\"}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"92a33316-c646-4c60-8a69-7c8d13d2b04b"],

Cell["DuckDBQuery[conn, \"SELECT * FROM fruit ORDER BY id\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"92ac0031-761b-434a-9734-04f1f1bc1942"],

Cell["DuckDBDisconnect[conn]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"af4499d8-f121-43dd-94c7-6ae8ba275a41"],

Cell["Reopening the same file shows the rows are still there:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"003d5b4a-cdd6-4f55-bf5a-f8a0ff2cb60e"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb:///\" <> file,
    DuckDBQuery[#, \"SELECT count(*) AS rows FROM fruit\"] &]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ea0faf4e-684f-44e5-8557-2f7d3ad9849c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Failures", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"75ee93d0-6a6b-4c90-89eb-465552186f8f"],

Cell["\<\
Errors from the engine arrive as Failure objects carrying DuckDB's own \
message, and propagate on their own.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bdbe18cf-1779-43d1-b15b-d602b6e31663"],

Cell["\<\
DuckDBExecute[\"duckdb://\", DuckDBQuery[#, \"SELECT * FROM no_such_table\"] \
&]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"63d50cf0-d072-4e8c-a11e-06ffd79e4bae"],

Cell["\<\
A handle that has been closed is no longer in the Rust-side registry:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9f12a8ca-447b-4754-b6d7-d127cae7ac94"],

Cell["\<\
With[{c = DuckDBConnect[]},
    DuckDBDisconnect[c];
    DuckDBQuery[c, \"SELECT 1\"]
]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"53a35628-3cbf-47f6-bf5e-3c2e6eee426e"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The raw library", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"766d7123-26d9-40ed-a4d2-5ecf659a29e8"],

Cell["\<\
The wrappers in Kernel/WolframExample.wl are a thin layer over an association \
of LibraryFunctions, keyed \"namespace::rust_name\". Anything without a \
wrapper is still one lookup away.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4e2c324d-0708-4b01-9f6d-73a9f7a4a4c7"],

Cell["Keys[WolframExampleFunctions[]]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"d5104840-4040-41d6-b074-6e2f53eae36d"],

Cell["\<\
inactive_sum builds an expression in Rust and returns it unevaluated:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8abeea72-06a2-4670-aebf-d85b848017f2"],

Cell["WolframExampleFunctions[][\"math::inactive_sum\"][{1, 2, 3}]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ab7caac5-3de8-41fa-9881-4866d63c99fb"],

Cell["\<\
Activate[WolframExampleFunctions[][\"math::inactive_sum\"][{1, 2, 3}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"9d063db8-2d2a-4c94-8152-5d528296b3f0"],

Cell["\<\
A panic on the Rust side is caught at the boundary and returned as a Failure \
\[AHat]\.80\.94 it does not take the kernel down:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d295fa0a-3daa-4566-b59a-a0b3d0f06216"],

Cell["WolframExampleFunctions[][\"math::panic\"][]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f4dbe8a3-8a07-4ff6-ac72-28bf5f919347"],

Cell["\<\
And the signatures of everything that was packaged, straight from the \
generated Artifacts.wl asset:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ea7e5cb2-c97b-48d3-bb49-95a703368c5c"],

Cell["\<\
Get[PacletObject[\"WolframExampleLib\"][\"AssetLocation\", \"Artifacts\"]] //
    Map[Query[{\"Name\", \"Signatures\"}]] // Dataset\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"07d039cb-8580-4c6e-b775-8b59ea260a95"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Rebuilding", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5d30ce60-945e-4486-a29b-4c0d57863d16"],

Cell["\<\
After editing the Rust source, rebuild from the paclet directory. The dylibs \
are content-hashed, so a rebuilt library gets a new file name \[AHat]\.80\.94 \
quit the kernel to pick it up.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5720c692-6744-46f7-bd15-2165638a24f0"],

Cell["\<\
ExternalEvaluate[{\"Shell\",
    \"ProcessDirectory\" -> \
FileNameJoin[{ParentDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]], \"WolframExample\"}],
    \"ProcessEnvironment\" -> <|\"PATH\" -> Environment[\"PATH\"]|>},
   \"cargo wl build --release\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"0cf888e6-2447-45e5-abdb-00d7eba4c7a3"]
}, Open  ]]
},
WindowTitle->"WolframExample Tour",
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Mac OS X ARM (64-bit) (May 6, 2026)",
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb",
ExpressionUUID->"d934e24d-2b59-4cb7-acdd-d2ec9039bcf2"
]
